  "answer": "This request has been filed before: sharing a custom region of a 4K or ultra-wide screen in Teams so you can swap apps in and out without switching shares. The past tickets were closed as duplicates of the general tracking issue (#279, and for newer tickets #43464), so there is no built-in PowerToys feature yet and you can follow those issues for progress. Teams itself does not support sharing a screen region, so a Teams-side fix would have to come from the Teams feedback portal. In the meantime, use the free 'Region to Share' app ([user]/RegionToShare, also in the Microsoft Store). Another user suggested pinning it inside a FancyZones zone, which makes it transparent so the windows behind it show through. You can then move any app into that zone while presenting."
 },
